 (parms full note)←StormGuard(parms error);signature;count;filename;state;problem;qdmx;now
⍝ The crash storm guard: decides whether a crash gets the full treatment. See `Misc/CrashStormGuard.md`.\\
⍝ `error` is the copy of `⎕DMX` taken by `Process`.\\
⍝ Returns `parms`, a Boolean that is 1 for the full treatment, and a note for the log entry and the
⍝ Windows event. With `stormGuard` 0 that is just `parms`, 1 and an empty note.\\
⍝ With `stormGuard` 1 it adds `stormSignature` and `stormCount` to `parms`.\\
⍝ Fails open: whatever goes wrong, the crash gets the full treatment and the note says why. A file
⍝ that cannot be read is replaced by a fresh one, so a damaged file does not disable the guard for good.\\
⍝ Requires that only one process writes to the error folder: `:Hold` does not reach across processes.
 full←1
 note←''
 :If parms.stormGuard
     signature←''
     count←0
     problem←''
     :Trap parms.trapInternalErrors/0
         signature←StormSignature error
         filename←parms.errorFolder,'/StormGuard.txt'
         :Trap parms.trapInternalErrors/0
             state←ReadStormFile filename
         :Else
             qdmx←⎕DMX
             problem←'could not read its file (',qdmx.EM,((0<≢qdmx.Message)/': ',qdmx.Message),') and started afresh'
             state←NewStormState
         :EndTrap
         now←UtcNow
         (state count full)←StormRule state signature now parms.stormCeiling parms.stormResetAfter
         filename WriteStormFile state
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
         problem←'failed (',qdmx.EM,((0<≢qdmx.Message)/': ',qdmx.Message),')'
     :EndTrap
     full∨←0<≢problem                           ⍝ Fail open
     parms.stormSignature←signature
     parms.stormCount←count
     :If 0<≢problem
         note←'Storm guard ',problem,'; full treatment'
     :Else
         note←'Storm guard: occurrence ',(⍕count),' of "',signature,'"'
         :If ~full
             note,←'; everything but the log entry and the Windows event held back'
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
